# Qt / QML Style Guidelines

Applies to all files under `qt_frontend/`.
See [TODO.md](../../docs/status-docs/TODO_SEAMLYLAYOUT_2.md) Phase 3 and onwards.

## C++ File Headers

All `.cpp` and `.h` files must start with:

```cpp
// project: SeamlyLayout
// author: slspencer, copyright 2026
// MIT License: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT
```

## QML File Headers

All `.qml` files must start with:

```qml
// project: SeamlyLayout
// author: slspencer, copyright 2026
// MIT License: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT
```

## C++ Naming Conventions

| Item | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Classes | `PascalCase` | `AppController`, `SettingsModel` |
| Methods / slots | `camelCase` | `importSvg()`, `processLayout()` |
| Signals | `camelCase`, past tense or noun | `importFinished()`, `errorOccurred()` |
| Properties | `camelCase` | `importedSvgPath`, `isLayoutReady` |
| Member variables | `m_camelCase` | `m_importedSvgPath`, `m_layoutReady` |
| Constants | `ALL_CAPS` | `MAX_ZOOM_LEVEL` |
| Local variables | `camelCase` | `svgPath`, `placedCount` |
| Files | `PascalCase` | `AppController.h`, `SettingsModel.cpp` |

## QML Naming Conventions

| Item | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Component files | `PascalCase.qml` | `SvgCanvas.qml`, `SeamlyButton.qml` |
| Component IDs | `camelCase` | `id: leftCanvas`, `id: settingsDialog` |
| Properties | `camelCase` | `property string svgSource` |
| Signals | `camelCase` | `signal importRequested(string path)` |
| Signal handlers | `on` + PascalCase | `onImportFinished:`, `onClicked:` |
| Singleton files | `PascalCase.qml` with `pragma Singleton` | `Theme.qml` |

## C++ Comments

- Use Doxygen-style `///` for all public class members, methods, and signals
- Use `//` for inline implementation comments
- `if`, `else`, `for`, `while`, `switch` closing braces must have a comment repeating the conditional

```cpp
/// @brief Loads an SVG file and exposes it to QML via importedSvgPath.
/// @param path Absolute file path to the SVG file.
void AppController::importSvg(const QString &path)
{
    if (path.isEmpty()) {
        // path is empty — emit error and return
        emit errorOccurred(QStringLiteral("No file path provided"));
        return;
    } // if path.isEmpty()
    // ...
} // AppController::importSvg
```

## QML Comments

- Use `//` for all inline comments
- Add a `// ComponentName.qml — brief description` comment on the first line after the header

## Signal / Slot Patterns

- Declare all signals in `.h` under `signals:` section
- Connect Qt signals to QML via `Q_PROPERTY` with `NOTIFY` or direct `QML_ELEMENT` exposure
- Use **queued connections** for cross-thread signals (worker → AppController → QML)
- Never block the main thread: all Rust FFI calls that may be slow go on a `QThread` worker

```cpp
// Worker thread emits result via queued connection
connect(worker, &LayoutWorker::layoutComplete,
        this,   &AppController::onLayoutComplete,
        Qt::QueuedConnection);
```

## Property Declaration Pattern

```cpp
class AppController : public QObject
{
    Q_OBJECT
    QML_ELEMENT

    /// @brief Path to the imported SVG file, empty if no file is loaded.
    Q_PROPERTY(QString importedSvgPath READ importedSvgPath NOTIFY importedSvgPathChanged)

public:
    /// @brief Returns the current imported SVG file path.
    QString importedSvgPath() const { return m_importedSvgPath; }

signals:
    void importedSvgPathChanged();
    void importFinished();
    void errorOccurred(QString message);

private:
    QString m_importedSvgPath;
};
```

## QML Component Pattern

```qml
// project: SeamlyLayout
// author: slspencer, copyright 2026
// MIT License: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT
// SeamlyButton.qml — Branded button matching the violet/gray palette

import QtQuick 6.11
import QtQuick.Controls 6.11

Button {
    id: root

    // Expose palette via Theme singleton
    background: Rectangle {
        color: root.hovered ? Theme.violet : Theme.violetMedium
        border.color: root.hovered ? Theme.grayLight : Theme.violetDark
        radius: 4
    }

    contentItem: Text {
        text: root.text
        color: Theme.grayLight
        font.pixelSize: 14
        horizontalAlignment: Text.AlignHCenter
        verticalAlignment: Text.AlignVCenter
    }
}
```

## CMakeLists.txt Conventions

- Use `qt_add_qml_module` for QML modules
- Use `qt_add_executable` for the application binary
- Use `target_link_libraries` with `PRIVATE` visibility for all Qt modules
- Place generated files in `${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/generated/`
- Include Rust FFI headers via `target_include_directories(app PRIVATE ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/../crates/ffi_bridge/include)`

## Do Not

- Use `QWidgets` for new UI — all UI must be QML-based
- Use Qt `staticlib` linking for Qt modules (violates LGPLv3)
- Call Rust FFI functions directly from QML — always go through a `QObject` C++ bridge
- Use `QString` raw pointers across the FFI boundary — convert to `const char*` at the C ABI layer
- Use GPL-only Qt modules (Qt Charts, Qt Data Visualization)

## Always

- Register C++ types with QML via `QML_ELEMENT` or `qmlRegisterType`
- Use `Q_INVOKABLE` for methods callable from QML
- Use `QVariantMap` for passing structured data between QML and C++
- Use the `output/` directory for Qt debug/intermediate files, matching Rust conventions
